This repository is open-source software (see LICENSE). It does not distribute a copy of the
Michigan Compiled Laws, and none is bundled with it: `fixtures/` contains only synthetic
"[FIXTURE]" text used by the test suite.

If you run your own instance, you will fetch statutory text yourself, from
https://legislature.mi.gov/documents/mcl/ (the Legislature's own machine-readable XML) and/or
the Legislature's website. Before you do:

- Read `docs/lsb-inquiry.md` and `docs/lsb-reply-2026-09-21.md` in this repository. They record
  a real written exchange with the Michigan Legislature (Legislative Service Bureau) about
  automated access, current as of 2026-09-21. Automated access was described as permitted, with
  a requested rate limit of at most 1 request per second (stated as subject to change), and
  storing/serving a copy was described as permitted with no specific wording requirements.
  This is not a license grant to you personally, is not legal advice, and terms can change --
  read the reply yourself and, if in doubt, ask the Legislature directly (contact information
  is in `docs/lsb-inquiry.md`).
- Identify your own crawler with your own contact information (`MLAW_USER_AGENT`), keep your
  request rate at or below what the Legislature has asked for, and do not remove or weaken the
  standing notice (`mlaw.config.NOTICE`) that this is an unofficial copy, subject to revision,
  and provided without warranties.
- Do not represent statutory text served by your instance as an official publication of the
  State of Michigan or the Michigan Legislature. Verify anything you rely on against the
  official source, especially for a filing or a deadline.

None of this is legal advice. If you intend to run a copy of this server for anyone beyond
yourself, have a lawyer familiar with your jurisdiction and use case review your terms of use.
